{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetW6SWHmVCyzkpkZdgTe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Error handling via exceptions: ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409), caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Error responses wrapped in `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }` envelope\n- Controllers use MockMvc tests with fluent assertions on status and jsonPath\n- Repositories are in-memory ConcurrentHashMap-based\n- Status transitions stored directly in the model\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Must add error code for CANCELLED shipment conflict\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add POST confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if logic is placed in wrong location\n- Incorrect HTTP status codes (need 409 for CANCELLED, 404 for missing)\n- Idempotency failure if CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED doesn't properly handle (requirement says \"retry must not fail\")\n- Adding new dependencies if I choose a wrong approach\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone — the requirement clearly specifies all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED, CANCELLED→409, missing→404) and all behaviors are well-defined.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum. This describes the state conflict when confirming a CANCELLED shipment (409 Conflict).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves shipment by ID; if missing, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with the new error code\n   - If status is `CREATED`, updates to `CONFIRMED` and saves\n   - If status is already `CONFIRMED`, returns it unchanged (saves again to be idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four tests:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment → moves to CONFIRMED, returns the shipment\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds, returns unchanged\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED error code\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment → returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Creating a separate `ConfirmShipmentService` class: Adds complexity without value. The domain logic is simple: validate state, update status, save. This is fine to keep in the controller following existing patterns (see OrderController).\n- Using a custom ShipmentStatus → request/response wrapper: Unnecessary. The existing Shipment model is returned as-is.\n- Adding a separate `confirmShipment` method in the repository: The repository's `save()` method is already sufficient.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | Shipment by ID | Save Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | 200 Shipment | repository.findById + repository.save |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | Shipment by ID | Save Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | 200 Shipment | repository.findById + repository.save |\n| CANCELLED → error | Shipment by ID | (none) | 409 ApiError | throw ConflictException (caught by GlobalExceptionHandler) |\n| Missing → error | (none) | (none) | 404 ApiError | throw ResourceNotFoundException (caught by GlobalExceptionHandler) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1**: \"confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\" — POST to confirm endpoint, verify 200 status, verify response shipment has status=CONFIRMED\n- **Test 2**: \"confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds\" — Create and confirm shipment, then confirm again, verify 200 status and unchanged response\n- **Test 3**: \"rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409\" — Insert CANCELLED shipment directly in repository, POST confirm, verify 409 status and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED error code\n- **Test 4**: \"rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404\" — POST confirm on missing ID, verify 404 status and SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3386,"cache_read_input_tokens":25585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3386},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dac01c70-feca-4186-b18a-b59f65b02b65","uuid":"8e6eb7d5-0d4e-4ee3-ae96-55936ffe9d5a","timestamp":"2026-09-09T20:33:11.542Z","request_id":"req_011CetW6RpbpUMkmfHQ8SuES"}
