{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetWAaTdioxqTmzzreKpm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! **Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** \n- Tests run: 17 (increased from 13 — the 4 new confirm endpoint tests pass)\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- Build: SUCCESS\n- Exit code: 0\n\nAll existing tests continue to pass, and all new tests pass.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ Existing build passes — BUILD SUCCESS, no compilation errors\n2. ✅ Existing tests pass — All 4 original OrderControllerTest tests pass; all 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests pass\n3. ✅ `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it — Test: \"confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\" verifies endpoint exists, transitions status, and returns saved shipment\n4. ✅ Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API — Uses same exception pattern (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) caught by GlobalExceptionHandler, wrapped in ApiError envelope\n5. ✅ A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused:\n   - Repeated confirm: Test \"confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds\" verifies idempotency (POST twice, both 200 OK)\n   - Cancelled rejected: Test \"rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with conflict\" verifies 409 + SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED\n   - Unknown id refused: Test \"rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with not found\" verifies 404 + SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n6. ✅ No new Maven dependency appears — Only edited .kt files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ No unrelated production file changes — Only modified ShipmentController.kt (to add confirm endpoint), Shipment model files unchanged except test, and ApiError.kt (added one enum value)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum (line 35, between SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS and VALIDATION_FAILED). This change was necessary to represent the 409 error case.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method (lines 57–72):\n   - Retrieves shipment by ID; throws ResourceNotFoundException if missing → 404\n   - Checks if status is CANCELLED; throws ConflictException if so → 409\n   - Creates a copy with status CONFIRMED and saves it\n   - Returns the saved shipment\n   - This endpoint handles all four cases from the requirement, including idempotency (both CREATED→CONFIRMED and CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED save and return the shipment)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 tests (lines 85–144):\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — Verifies 200 OK and status change\n   - `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds` — Verifies idempotency\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with conflict` — Verifies 409 and correct error code\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with not found` — Verifies 404 and correct error code\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All criteria met, no files changed that shouldn't be, no dependencies added.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Implement POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm to transition shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED, allow retries, reject CANCELLED with 409, and return 404 for missing shipments.\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt — added SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED error code to enum\n              ShipmentController.kt — added @PostMapping confirm() endpoint with state validation\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 4 new tests for confirm endpoint (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotency, CANCELLED rejection, not-found rejection)\n\nTests         Test 1: \"confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\" — verifies status transition and 200 OK\n              Test 2: \"confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds\" — verifies idempotency (retry succeeds)\n              Test 3: \"rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with conflict\" — verifies 409 status and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED error code\n              Test 4: \"rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with not found\" — verifies 404 status and SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service/)\n              Result: Tests run: 17, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0, BUILD SUCCESS\n              All 4 new tests pass, all 13 existing tests pass, no compilation errors\n\nNot done      (none — all acceptance criteria met, verification passed)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3389,"cache_read_input_tokens":34762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3389},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dac01c70-feca-4186-b18a-b59f65b02b65","uuid":"b8281a58-5db7-493e-ab8d-bdb98016e992","timestamp":"2026-09-09T20:33:58.141Z","request_id":"req_011CetWAZnCXMb4yUaTV5UJE"}
